[THOUGHT] Unvaccinated status significantly increases risk for vaccine-preventable diseases (e.g., measles, varicella, rubella), though absence of sick contacts makes transmission less likely — unless incubation period hasn’t yet passed. No travel or tick/animal exposure lowers concern for rickettsial or zoonotic causes. Next, Domain 7: targeted physical examination. Since history is limited in specificity, direct observation is essential. I must request objective assessment of rash morphology (macular/papular/vesicular/petechial), blanching, distribution (especially palms/soles), and mucocutaneous features (conjunctivae, oral cavity, lips, extremities) — all critical to differentiate diagnoses. Also need vital signs (temp, HR, RR, capillary refill) to assess severity.

[TEST] Please perform and report:  
- Temperature (current), heart rate, respiratory rate, and capillary refill time;  
- Rash description: color, morphology (e.g., macules, papules, vesicles, petechiae), distribution (trunk, face, extremities, palms/soles), and whether lesions blanch with pressure;  
- Conjunctival exam: presence of injection or exudate;  
- Oral exam: pharyngeal erythema, tonsillar exudate, strawberry tongue, lip fissuring, or buccal enanthem;  
- Extremity exam: edema, erythema, or desquamation of hands/feet.

